WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.200
Hey Youtubers! It's Charlie.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.200
Hopefully you guys have had a chance to see Star Wars - Episode 7 this weekend.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.260
Maybe once, maybe like five times.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.700
But, I thought it would be fun to do a video just about the dark side of the force

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.400
and the state of the things in the new trilogy, versus what happened in the past.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.180
We are going to be talking about spoilers from the movie

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.000
So just careful for *SPOILERS* if you haven't seen it yet!

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.400
We're going to be talking about the Knights of Ren, the Sith, and just the dark side of the force in general.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.500
So I'm going to start with this quote from Maz Kanata -  she kind of sets the stage for what's going on with the

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.590
dark side of the force and just evil in
general in the galaxy.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:36.200
She's about a thousand years old, as told by Han Solo, and says "I've seen darkness take many forms -

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.100
the Sith, the Empire, now it's calling
itself the First Order."

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.300
Now, the First Order and the Knights of Ren
are two completely different things.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.070
The thing of them is sharing the same type
of relationship that the Sith did with

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:52.140
the Empire. Like the Emperor was part of
the Sith - he created the Empire.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.440
That's why I feel like Snoke is
associated with the Knights of Ren, who

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.890
led to the creation of the First Order.
Now obviously there's a lot we don't

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.000
know about Snoke. We know less about him than almost any other character right now.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.430
It's kind of the same way after
episode 4, after A New Hope, we really

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.139
didn't know anything about the Emperor
either.

00:01:07.139 --> 00:01:12.300
Only that Darth Vader, this you know seemingly really powerful evil person, had a master himself.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.579
So in the movie, Snoke says, "Even you,
Master of the Knights of Ren, haven't

00:01:17.579 --> 00:01:19.799
faced a test like this before."

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:23.100
Rey has that force vision when she touches the lightsaber that shows her

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.069
Kylo Ren's characters surrounded by a bunch
of dark figures.

00:01:26.069 --> 00:01:30.000
I think those are the Knights of Ren - the
actual people that are part of the Knights of Ren.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:33.209
So what I think JJ Abrams has done is
move things away from George Lucas's

00:01:33.209 --> 00:01:37.109
reliance on the Sith as a group of dark
side force users.

00:01:37.109 --> 00:01:40.649
It's like the way different religions of
of real-world earth describe their

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:43.590
ultimate deity. Like everyone has a
slightly different description different

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:47.639
interpretation of religion. But I still
think it all flows from the same source,

00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:51.539
and remember Luke was trying to find the
original Jedi Temple.

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:55.229
Now in the expanded universe, there's
actually a story about the beginning of

00:01:55.229 --> 00:01:58.499
the Jedi, but they threw out the
expanded universe, so we can't really use

00:01:58.499 --> 00:02:01.499
any of those stories as theory crafting,
like whatever they're doing with this

00:02:01.499 --> 00:02:05.600
new trilogy, completely different from
what the comics did with the origin of the Jedi.

00:02:05.669 --> 00:02:08.729
So here's my question for you guys, let
me know in the comments below, do you

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:14.700
think that Supreme Leader Snoke and Luke Skywalker, as part of like the arc of the Force in the new trilogy,

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:21.900
are on similar paths. Like their story will get back to the origins of the Jedi and the origins of the Force.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.100
When you look back to the original
trilogy, like what would Emperor Palpatine

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.500
have done if he had truly conquered the galaxy and eradicated the Jedi. Would you have seen

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.400
a new order of Sith rise up, or would it have remained the George Lucas "rule of two" thing.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.400
In case you guys didn't know too - whenever George Lucas sold Lucasfilm to Disney,

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.950
one of his conditions was that he would be allowed input on the new films.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.980
So he gave an outline for the new
trilogy, and it was only read by like the

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:51.180
top three Disney executives. Only three
people at Disney read George Lucas'

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.200
plans for the new trilogy. They
ultimately decided to throw that out and

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.100
that's when they decided to kind of throw out the expanded universe too - go in a different direction.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.400
You have the Knights of Ren instead of the Sith, you have the Resistance instead of the Rebellion.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:06.720
I'm actually, I'm fairly fascinated to
find out exactly what was in George

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.410
Lucas's outline. But largely, most people
think that it was just more focused on

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.740
younger characters. Just like the
prequels were focused on younger

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:17.220
characters. So, by all accounts, I think
the Lucasfilm story group did the right

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.680
thing when they got rid of George Lucas's ideas.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.950
I mean they also kinda through the Sith
out in terms of like a bad group of

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:26.400
dark side force users, but now we have
this new group to learn about.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.910
So presumably, in like you know 20 years or
however longer it takes for them to make

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.300
a new trilogy, we might even see like a
new interpretation of the dark side of the force.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.800
Make no mistake, episode 9 is not going
to be the last saga film.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.459
They're gonna make a new star wars film
every single year 'til the end of time.

00:03:41.459 --> 00:03:44.790
And when I say saga films, i'm just talking
about main trilogy. You have like the

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.130
spin-off films like Rogue One, that will be next year.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.280
Those will fill in the gaps between
saga films. And if you guys didn't know

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:57.000
Kathleen Kennedy did say that these new saga films, episodes 7, 8, 9, will follow the Skywalker family.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.300
So when you're thinking about character back stories,

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.150
just think about the Skywalker family being very, very important.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.400
I know we're all still wondering who Rey is, and then there's really like a couple of really clear choices.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:12.300
You know, is she a Skywalker? Is she a Solo?
Is she somebody completely different?

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.840
I feel like any direction they go is
fine, because her character so amazing

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.800
though that you might not even care by
the time they actually explain it.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.540
Like you'd just be so in love with Daisy Ridley.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:25.200
That's what I feel like these new films
get right that the prequels did not.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.280
Even if you like the spectacle of the
prequels, like there were some

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:32.090
amazing big scenes in the prequels, some
really cool stuff that happened.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:35.600
I feel like the characters just weren't
there in the way they are these new films.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.090
But back to Kylo Ren, Master of the
Knights of Ren.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:42.350
Is there anybody who feels like this new
trilogy isn't all about the redemption

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:45.950
of Kylo Ren? I mean obviously it's a much
bigger story than that, but that's the

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:52.300
central family arc - bring Ben home. And
who else just loves that he's named after Ben Kenobi.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:55.580
It's a perfectly timed bomb to blow up your heart.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.669
I kept wondering what Kylo Ren's real
name was going to be. You know I was so

00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:02.120
happy when I heard Han Solo call that
out. I mean obviously it comes before a

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.240
really cry-worthy scene. But, it was such a
perfect moment.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:09.020
So moving to episode 8 territory, we're
probably going to see a lot more of the

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:14.500
actual Knights of Ren, because Supreme Leader Snoke is going to be finishing Kylo Ren's training.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:19.400
And as much as episode 7 rhyme visually and thematically with episode 4,

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.700
I feel like episode 8 is going to be
uncharted territory. So don't expect it

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:27.600
to follow the story beats of Empire as much as
episode 7 follows the story beats of episode 4.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.600
I am so excited to see what Ryan Johnson
does with these characters.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.460
And Daisy Ridley has actually said that she's read the
episode 8 script, so the script is

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:37.970
done. And they've already filmed again,
you know that place where Luke Skywalker,

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.220
where Rey's character finds Luke
Skywalker,

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:44.120
they've already been back there to film
scenes for episode 8. Would you not be so

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:48.050
upset if they just skipped over that
last moment with Rey trying to hand the

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:51.100
